' ─────────────────── Note ───────────────────
note right of PayrollServiceImpl
  BR-17 (Payroll Approval Authority):
  enforced in SecurityConfig — /api/v1/payroll/**
  hasAnyRole("MANAGER", "ADMIN").
  The approver is taken from the JWT principal,
  NOT from the request body, so it cannot be spoofed.
  BR-09 (No Hard Delete): approve() sets locked = true
  on EVERY line in the same transaction as the status
  change; afterwards updateItem() and generateDraft()
  both refuse the period.
end note

note bottom of PayrollItem
  Composition (filled diamond): @OneToMany with
  cascade = ALL + orphanRemoval = true —
  a payroll line cannot exist outside its period.

  staffType + staffRefId form a "polymorphic" foreign key
  of type Long; it is NOT mapped as an association to
  Doctor/Staff, hence the conditional dependencies above.

  netPay is always derived as baseSalary
  + performanceBonus - deduction,
  never taken directly from the client.
end note

note bottom of PayrollPeriod
  status is a String: {DRAFT, APPROVED}
  (not yet extracted into an enum in the current code).
  approve() has an idempotency guard: approving twice
  throws IllegalStateException so approvedBy / approvedAt
  are never overwritten.
end note

note left of PayrollController
  Deviations from SRS UC-54, need a decision:
  1. POST-3 "export the payroll to Accounting/Admin":
     NO export endpoint exists in the code yet.
  2. E-1 "an adjustment beyond the variance threshold
     requires a mandatory note": the code checks no
     threshold and the note stays optional.
  3. BR-17 says ONLY the Clinic Manager, but the current
     configuration also lets ADMIN approve.
  4. The API returns Map<String,Object> instead of DTOs
     (no PayrollPeriodResponse/PayrollItemResponse),
     so there is no explicit data contract for the FE.
end note

note as N_ALT
  ALT-1 (Reject & recalculate) is implemented by calling
  generateDraft() again: it wipes the previous lines of a
  DRAFT period and rebuilds them from activity data
  (Doctor: count of COMPLETED Appointments in the period;
  Staff: seeded with the base salary only, to be adjusted
  manually). This delete only ever touches a DRAFT period,
  so it does not violate BR-09.
end note
N_ALT .. PayrollServiceImpl

@enduml
